Events and semaphores call the kernel only for the waiters they have (Switch): a signal or release wakes its own address only when a thread sleeps in its Wait, and the WaitMultiple polls only when one looks at that object. Run 35 at stock clocks had 60-80 thousand svcSignalToAddress a second and the audio worker woken 28 thousand times a second by other objects' signals.

